sion. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nएक था मोटा राजा (Hindi)\nराजा दौड़ा कुत्ते के पीछे\nयह पठन स्तर १ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो पढ़ना शुरू कर रहे हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%8f%e0%a4%95-%e0%a4%a5%e0%a4%be-%e0%a4%ae%e0%a5%8b%e0%a4%9f%e0%a4%be-%e0%a4%b0%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%9c%e0%a4%be-2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"ed3ef931b7bf7f69"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"एक था मोटा राजा\nएक राजा था। वह बहुत मोटा था।\nउस मोटे राजा के पास एक पतला कुत्ता था । एक दिन मोटा राजा और उसका पतला कुत्ता  सैर करने गए।\nकुत्ते ने एक चिड़िया को देखा। वह कुत्ता उस चिड़िया के पीछे दौड़ा।\nराजा भी कुत्ते के पीछे दौड़ा।\nवो दोनों दौड़े -भागे और बहुत दिनों तक दौड़ते भागते रहे।\nआखिरकार राजा ने  कुत्ते को पकड़ ही लिया।\nदौड़ दौड़ कर मोटा राजा भी कुत्ते की तरह पतला हो गया।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":19,"title":"एक था मोटा राजा"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-21-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"एक था मोटा राजा","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:21","title":"एक था मोटा राजा","author":"Parismita","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Parismita\nIllustrator: Parismita\nTranslator: Seema Biswas\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: एक था मोटा राजा is translated by Seema Biswas . The © for this translation lies with Seema Biswas , 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' Fat King Thin Dog ' , by Parismita . © Pratham Books , 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: King catching a dog , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: Fat King , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: Fat King walking with a thin dog , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Dog chasing a bird , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: King chasing a dog , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: Tired king running after a dog , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: King catching a dog , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: Thin King and dog , by Parismita © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nएक था मोटा राजा (Hindi)\nराजा दौड़ा कुत्ते के पीछे\nयह पठन स्तर १ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो पढ़ना शुरू कर रहे हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%8f%e0%a4%95-%e0%a4%a5%e0%a4%be-%e0%a4%ae%e0%a5%8b%e0%a4%9f%e0%a4%be-%e0%a4%b0%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%9c%e0%a4%be/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"ed3ef931b7bf7f69"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"एक था मोटा राजा\nएक राजा था। वह बहुत मोटा था।\nउस मोटे राजा के पास एक पतला कुत्ता था । एक दिन मोटा राजा और उसका पतला कुत्ता  सैर करने गए।\nकुत्ते ने एक चिड़िया को देखा। वह कुत्ता उस चिड़िया के पीछे दौड़ा।\nराजा भी कुत्ते के पीछे दौड़ा।\nवो दोनों दौड़े -भागे और बहुत दिनों तक दौड़ते भागते रहे।\nआखिरकार राजा ने  कुत्ते को पकड़ ही लिया।\nदौड़ दौड़ कर मोटा राजा भी कुत्ते की तरह पतला हो गया।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":20,"title":"एक था मोटा राजा"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-22-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:22","title":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर","author":"Madhuri Purandare","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Madhuri Purandare\nIllustrator: Madhuri Purandare\nTranslator: Arti Smit\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर is translated by Arti Smit . The © for this translation lies with Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' एकशे सदतिसावा पाय ' , by Madhuri Purandare . © Pratham Books , 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nOther Credits:\n'Ek Sau Saintisvan Paer' has been published on StoryWeaver by Pratham Books. The development of this book has been supported by HDFC Asset Management Company Limited- a joint Venture with Standard Life Investments. www.prathambooks.org\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: A beautiful colourful forest with a variety of trees , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: Sun shining on trees and plants , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: A bird chirping on a tree branch , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Millipede sleeping under a leaf with birds flying around , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: A millipede sleeping under a leaf with birds chirping on a tree branch , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: A millipede letting out a big yawn in the morning , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: A millipede crawling in one scene, and then talking to someone in the other , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: A sparrow and a millipede talking to each other , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Sparrow flying away, and a millipede on the ground , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Honeybees and dragonflies flying in separate groups , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: A snail crawling slowly and two butterflies flying together , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: A millipede crawling towards us with lots of trees behind it , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: A millipede crying in front of a spider hanging on its web , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 14: A millipede and a spider , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 15: Spider fixing the millipede's leg using its silk threads , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 16: A smiling millipede and a spider on the web , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nएक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर (Hindi)\nएक गोजर को चोट लगी है। उसे मदद की ज़रूरत है। अब वह कौन सा पैर है, जिसे मदद की ज़रूरत है? पेश है एक बाल साहित्य पुरस्कार विजेता की एक नई रोचक सचित्र पुस्तक!\nयह पठन स्तर २ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो सरल शब्द पढ़ लेते हैं और थोड़ी मदद से नए शब्द भी पढ़ सकते हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%8f%e0%a4%95-%e0%a4%b8%e0%a5%8c-%e0%a4%b8%e0%a5%88%e0%a4%82%e0%a4%a4%e0%a5%80%e0%a4%b8%e0%a4%b5%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%81-%e0%a4%aa%e0%a5%88%e0%a4%b0-2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"502c5c9a92ab65fb"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर\nयह एक नए दिन की शुरूआत थी।\nजंगल पर सूरज की कोमल\nकिरणें फैल रही थीं।\nपंछी जाग चुके थे।\nएक गोजर एक बड़े से भूरे पत्ते के भीतर\nख़ुमारी में दुबकी हुई थी।\nचिड़ियों की चहचहाट ने उसे जगा दिया।\n“जाओ यहाँ से! मुझे सोने दो!” वह बुदबुदाई।\n“मैं जानती हूँ, सुबह हो चुकी है।\nतुम हर रोज़ इसके लिए शोर ना किया करो।”\nउसने चिड़ियों से कहा।\nगोजर पत्ते के भीतर से बाहर निकलकर आई।\nउसने अपने पहले पंद्रह जोड़े पैरों को खींचा।\nउसके बाद उसने लंबी जम्हाई ली।\n“कितनी भूख लगी है मुझे,” गोजर\nबोली और इधर-उधर नज़रें घुमाकर\nभोजन की खोज करने लगी।\nअपनी हड़बड़ाहट में वह एक बड़े पत्थर\nसे जा टकराई और गिर पड़ी।\n“हे ईश्वर! ओह!! मेरा एक पैर टूट गया!”\nवह चिल्लाई।\nपास ही एक नन्ही गौरैया दाना चुग रही थी।\n“अरे तुमने एक पैर तोड़ लिया? अगर मेरे पास इतने पैर होते तो मैं भी एक तोड़ लेती! देखो! देखो मुझे!! मेरे दो पैर हैं। एक दूसरे के साथ चलता है। कोई परेशानी नहीं! आसान!”\nवह इतरा कर बोली। “और इतनी जल्दबाज़ी किसलिए?”\n“क्या तुम मेरी मदद कर सकोगी?” गोजर ने पूछा।\n“इतनी सुबह! नहीं मैडम, मुझे मा़फ़ करें!\nमुझे अभी काम करने हैं।”\nगौरैया बोली और वहाँ से फुर्र हो गई।\nगोजर ने मधुमक्खियों से मदद माँगी।\nलेकिन वे भी फूलों से मधु इकट्ठा करने में व्यस्त थीं।\n“तुम्हारे पास बहुत सारे पैर हैं,” तितली बोली।\n“अगर एक टूट भी गया तो उसकी इतनी परवाह क्यों करती हो। बंद करो ये सब नाटक!”\nघोंघे ने सलाह दी, “तुम बहुत लापरवाह हो!\nतुम्हें इस तरह चलना चाहिए- धी...रे... धी....रे...।”\nइन बातों से गोजर अब बहुत दुखी हो गई।\n“उहूँ! उहूँ! कोई मेरी मदद करना नहीं चाहता!\nमैं फिर से पहले की तरह चलना चाहती हूँ।”\nवह सुबकने लगी।\nएक मकड़ा अपने जाल पर खुशी-खुशी\nझूल रहा था। उसने गोजर को रोते हुए देखा।\n“ओ मेरी नन्ही दोस्त! तुम्हें क्या हुआ,\nजो तुम इतनी सुबह-सुबह रो रही हो?” वह बोला।\n“मेरा एक पैर टूट गया और मुझे तकली़फ़ हो रही है।\nक्या तुम मेरी मदद कर सकोगे?” गोजर ने पूछा।\n“अरे, हाँ! मैं तुम्हारी मदद कर सकता हूँ।\nलेकिन तुम्हारे इतने सारे पैरों में से मैं टूटा पैर कैसे खोजूँ?\nमैं केवल आठ तक गिन सकता हूँ।” मकड़ा बोला।\n“ठीक है, मेरे साथ गिनो,” गोजर बोली,\n“एक... सात... तेईस....\nअट्ठावन.... ब्यानवे... एक सौ पंद्रह....\nएक सौ और आह! यही है मेरा टूटा पैर!\nमेरा एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर!”\nमकड़ा जाले से झूलता हुआ नीचे गोजर के पास उतरा।\nवह उसके टूटे पैर के चारों ओर घूमा...\nघूमता रहा और अपने जाले के रेशमी धागे से उसे बाँध दिया।\n“अब तुम बेहतर महसूस कर रही हो?” उसने पूछा।\nगोजर ख़ुश होकर मुस्कराने लगी।\n“धन्यवाद, प्रिय मकड़े! मैं नहीं जानती\nकि तुम्हारे बिना मैं क्या करती!”\n“अपना ख़याल रखो, नन्ही गोजर! अब किसी\nबड़ी चीज़ से टकराना मत। टाटा!” मकड़े ने कहा।\n“टाटा!” गोजर ख़ुश होकर बोली।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":21,"title":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-23-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:23","title":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर","author":"Madhuri Purandare","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Madhuri Purandare\nIllustrator: Madhuri Purandare\nTranslator: Arti Smit\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर is translated by Arti Smit . The © for this translation lies with Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' एकशे सदतिसावा पाय ' , by Madhuri Purandare . © Pratham Books , 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nOther Credits:\n'Ek Sau Saintisvan Paer' has been published on StoryWeaver by Pratham Books. The development of this book has been supported by HDFC Asset Management Company Limited- a joint Venture with Standard Life Investments. www.prathambooks.org\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: A beautiful colourful forest with a variety of trees , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: Sun shining on trees and plants , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: A bird chirping on a tree branch , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Millipede sleeping under a leaf with birds flying around , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: A millipede sleeping under a leaf with birds chirping on a tree branch , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: A millipede letting out a big yawn in the morning , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: A millipede crawling in one scene, and then talking to someone in the other , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: A sparrow and a millipede talking to each other , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Sparrow flying away, and a millipede on the ground , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Honeybees and dragonflies flying in separate groups , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: A snail crawling slowly and two butterflies flying together , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: A millipede crawling towards us with lots of trees behind it , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: A millipede crying in front of a spider hanging on its web , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 14: A millipede and a spider , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 15: Spider fixing the millipede's leg using its silk threads , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 16: A smiling millipede and a spider on the web , by Madhuri Purandare © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nएक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर (Hindi)\nएक गोजर को चोट लगी है। उसे मदद की ज़रूरत है। अब वह कौन सा पैर है, जिसे मदद की ज़रूरत है? पेश है एक बाल साहित्य पुरस्कार विजेता की एक नई रोचक सचित्र पुस्तक!\nयह पठन स्तर २ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो सरल शब्द पढ़ लेते हैं और थोड़ी मदद से नए शब्द भी पढ़ सकते हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%8f%e0%a4%95-%e0%a4%b8%e0%a5%8c-%e0%a4%b8%e0%a5%88%e0%a4%82%e0%a4%a4%e0%a5%80%e0%a4%b8%e0%a4%b5%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%81-%e0%a4%aa%e0%a5%88%e0%a4%b0/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"502c5c9a92ab65fb"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर\nयह एक नए दिन की शुरूआत थी।\nजंगल पर सूरज की कोमल\nकिरणें फैल रही थीं।\nपंछी जाग चुके थे।\nएक गोजर एक बड़े से भूरे पत्ते के भीतर\nख़ुमारी में दुबकी हुई थी।\nचिड़ियों की चहचहाट ने उसे जगा दिया।\n“जाओ यहाँ से! मुझे सोने दो!” वह बुदबुदाई।\n“मैं जानती हूँ, सुबह हो चुकी है।\nतुम हर रोज़ इसके लिए शोर ना किया करो।”\nउसने चिड़ियों से कहा।\nगोजर पत्ते के भीतर से बाहर निकलकर आई।\nउसने अपने पहले पंद्रह जोड़े पैरों को खींचा।\nउसके बाद उसने लंबी जम्हाई ली।\n“कितनी भूख लगी है मुझे,” गोजर\nबोली और इधर-उधर नज़रें घुमाकर\nभोजन की खोज करने लगी।\nअपनी हड़बड़ाहट में वह एक बड़े पत्थर\nसे जा टकराई और गिर पड़ी।\n“हे ईश्वर! ओह!! मेरा एक पैर टूट गया!”\nवह चिल्लाई।\nपास ही एक नन्ही गौरैया दाना चुग रही थी।\n“अरे तुमने एक पैर तोड़ लिया? अगर मेरे पास इतने पैर होते तो मैं भी एक तोड़ लेती! देखो! देखो मुझे!! मेरे दो पैर हैं। एक दूसरे के साथ चलता है। कोई परेशानी नहीं! आसान!”\nवह इतरा कर बोली। “और इतनी जल्दबाज़ी किसलिए?”\n“क्या तुम मेरी मदद कर सकोगी?” गोजर ने पूछा।\n“इतनी सुबह! नहीं मैडम, मुझे मा़फ़ करें!\nमुझे अभी काम करने हैं।”\nगौरैया बोली और वहाँ से फुर्र हो गई।\nगोजर ने मधुमक्खियों से मदद माँगी।\nलेकिन वे भी फूलों से मधु इकट्ठा करने में व्यस्त थीं।\n“तुम्हारे पास बहुत सारे पैर हैं,” तितली बोली।\n“अगर एक टूट भी गया तो उसकी इतनी परवाह क्यों करती हो। बंद करो ये सब नाटक!”\nघोंघे ने सलाह दी, “तुम बहुत लापरवाह हो!\nतुम्हें इस तरह चलना चाहिए- धी...रे... धी....रे...।”\nइन बातों से गोजर अब बहुत दुखी हो गई।\n“उहूँ! उहूँ! कोई मेरी मदद करना नहीं चाहता!\nमैं फिर से पहले की तरह चलना चाहती हूँ।”\nवह सुबकने लगी।\nएक मकड़ा अपने जाल पर खुशी-खुशी\nझूल रहा था। उसने गोजर को रोते हुए देखा।\n“ओ मेरी नन्ही दोस्त! तुम्हें क्या हुआ,\nजो तुम इतनी सुबह-सुबह रो रही हो?” वह बोला।\n“मेरा एक पैर टूट गया और मुझे तकली़फ़ हो रही है।\nक्या तुम मेरी मदद कर सकोगे?” गोजर ने पूछा।\n“अरे, हाँ! मैं तुम्हारी मदद कर सकता हूँ।\nलेकिन तुम्हारे इतने सारे पैरों में से मैं टूटा पैर कैसे खोजूँ?\nमैं केवल आठ तक गिन सकता हूँ।” मकड़ा बोला।\n“ठीक है, मेरे साथ गिनो,” गोजर बोली,\n“एक... सात... तेईस....\nअट्ठावन.... ब्यानवे... एक सौ पंद्रह....\nएक सौ और आह! यही है मेरा टूटा पैर!\nमेरा एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर!”\nमकड़ा जाले से झूलता हुआ नीचे गोजर के पास उतरा।\nवह उसके टूटे पैर के चारों ओर घूमा...\nघूमता रहा और अपने जाले के रेशमी धागे से उसे बाँध दिया।\n“अब तुम बेहतर महसूस कर रही हो?” उसने पूछा।\nगोजर ख़ुश होकर मुस्कराने लगी।\n“धन्यवाद, प्रिय मकड़े! मैं नहीं जानती\nकि तुम्हारे बिना मैं क्या करती!”\n“अपना ख़याल रखो, नन्ही गोजर! अब किसी\nबड़ी चीज़ से टकराना मत। टाटा!” मकड़े ने कहा।\n“टाटा!” गोजर ख़ुश होकर बोली।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":22,"title":"एक सौ सैंतीसवाँ पैर"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-24-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कचरे का बादल","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:24","title":"कचरे का बादल","author":"Karanjeet Kaur","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Karanjeet Kaur\nIllustrator: Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi\nTranslator: Poonam S. Kudesia\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: कचरे का बादल is translated by Poonam S. Kudesia . The © for this translation lies with Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' A Cloud of Trash ' , by Karanjeet Kaur . © Pratham Books , 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nOther Credits:\nThis book was first published on StoryWeaver by Pratham Books. The development of this book has been supported by Oracle. Art Director: Vinayak Varma\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: A girl running away from a cloud of waste , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: A sad girl , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: A girl being teased in school , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: A girl looking at a cloud of trash , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: A girl hiding behind a bench , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: A sad, lonely girl , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: A girl littering , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: An unhappy girl , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: A girl looking scared from under a blanket , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: A girl trying to get rid of trash , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThe development of this book has been supported by Oracle.\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: A girl crushing a plastic bottle , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: A girl scolding a boy for littering , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: A girl eating at the table, a woman throwing away plastic bags , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 14: A girl picking up trash from the street , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 15: A cheerful girl playing , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 16: Children playing with balloons and a kite , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 17: A girl crying , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 18: A girl standing behind a trash bin , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 19: Mixed trash , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThe development of this book has been supported by Oracle.\nकचरे का बादल (Hindi)\nचीकू के सिर पर कचरे का बादल मँडरा रहा है जिसकी वजह से वह दुनिया की सबसे दुखी लड़की हो गई। यह शानदार कहानी पढ़िए और जानिए कि चीकू ने कचरे के डरावने बादल से छुटकारा कैसे पाया।\nयह पठन स्तर २ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो सरल शब्द पढ़ लेते हैं और थोड़ी मदद से नए शब्द भी पढ़ सकते हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%9a%e0%a4%b0%e0%a5%87-%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%be-%e0%a4%ac%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a6%e0%a4%b2-2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"063f0d3c37bd1021"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"कचरे का बादल\nअपनी सारी दोस्तों के बीच चीकू बहुत दुखी थी।\nवो अपनी क्लास की सबसे दुखी लड़की थी।\nशायद वो दुनिया की सबसे दुखी लड़की थी।\nदोस्त? चीकू का अब कोई दोस्त नहीं था।\nचीकू के साथ कोई खेलना नहीं चाहता था।\nक्योंकि उसके सिर पर हमेशा एक बादल मँडराता।\nकचरे का एक बादल ।\nसंतरे के छिलके और बिस्कुट के खाली लिफ़ाफ़े,\nटूटे खिलौने, और पेंसिल की छीलन,\nप्लास्टिक की टेढ़ी-मेढ़ी बोतलें,\nऔर रंग-बिरँगी थैलियाँ,\nऔर इन सब पर भिनभिनाते मक्खियों के झुंड।\nकोई भी बच्चा ऐसी लड़की के साथ नहीं खेलना चाहता था जिसके सिर पर हमेशा कचरे का बादल मँडराता हो।\nकहीं कोई केले का छिल्का उसके सर पर गिर पड़े तो? छी!\nचीकू तो छुपम-छुपाई तक भी नहीं खेल सकती थी।\nक्योंकि बादल उसका पता बता देता था।\nएक दिन वो सोना से बोली, \"हम साथ-साथ स्कूल चलते हैं।\" सोना तो फ़ौरन दूर भाग गई।\n\"क्या मैं तुम्हारा पेंसिल शार्पनर इस्तेमाल कर लूँ?\" उसने स्वीटी से पूछा।\nस्वीटी मुँह चिढ़ाते हुए अपनी जगह बदल कर आशा के पास बैठ गई।\nचीकू को खाना भी अकेले खाना पड़ा।\nचीकू जानती थी कि उसे अम्मा का कहना मानना  चाहिए था।\nअम्मा हमेशा उसे कूड़ा फैलाने से मना करती थी।\n\"सड़क पर केले का  छिलका मत फेंको।\"\n\"बिस्कुट के खाली लिफ़ाफ़े कूड़ेदान में डालो।\"\nलेकिन चीकू ने उनकी बात नहीं मानी। वह हँसती रही और कूड़ा फैलाती रही।\nफिर एक दिन अम्मा को बहुत गुस्सा आ गया, उसने कहा, \"देखना अब यह कूड़ा हमेशा तुम्हारे साथ ही रहेगा!\" चीकू हँसती रही।\nअगले दिन जब चीकू सो कर उठी तो चारों तरफ मक्खियाँ भिनभिना रही थी, हर तरफ बदबू ही बदबू थी।\nसाथ ही सिर पर कचरे का बादल मँडरा रहा था।\nअम्मा की बात सच साबित हुई और उसके बाद चीकू हँसना बस भूल ही गई!\nचीकू ने भागना चाहा ।\nलेकिन कचरे का वो बादल हर जगह उसका पीछा करता रहा ।\nचीकू ने एक झाड़ू लेकर बादल को हटाने की कोशिश की,\nलेकिन वह उसे हटा नहीं सकी ।\nचीकू ने भरपूर कोशिश की!\nउसने चीख-चीख कर बादल से हटने को कहा।\nउसने तो बादल को कूड़ेदान में फेंकने की भी\nकोशिश की।\nलेकिन कचरे का बादल हटा ही नहीं।\nतब चीकू हो गयी बहुत दुखी।\nइसके बाद चीकू ने बाला को देखा सड़क पर केले का छिलका फेंकते हुए।\nचीकू को गुस्सा आ गया। क्या बाला को मेरे सिर पर कचरे का बादल नहीं दिख रहा?\nवो चिल्लाई, \"अरे बुदधू, छिलके को सड़क पर मत फेंको, कोई फिसल जाएगा!\"\nकचरे के बादल से डर कर, बाला ने, छिलके को कूड़ेदान में फेंक दिया।\nअगले दिन, कचरे का वह बादल थोड़ा सा छोटा हो गया!\nचीकू ने सोचा, \"अरे ऐसा कैसे हुआ?\"\nफिर चीकू ने देखा, कि रमा आंटी, प्लास्टिक की थैलियों को फेंक रहीं थीं।\nचीकू ने कहा, \"आंटी, थैलियों को उठाकर दोबारा इस्तेमाल कीजिए।\"\nरीमा आंटी थैलियाँ उठाकर वहाँ से चली गई! अगले दिन जब चीकू सो कर उठी, तो बादल और भी छोटा हो गया था।चीकू मुस्कराई, वह समझ गई थी कि उसे क्या करना है।\nफिर जब भी कोई बिस्कुट का पैकेट/लिफ़ाफ़ा या पेंसिल की छीलन फेंकता चीकू उसे रोक देती।\nप्लास्टिक की हर बेकार बोतल उठाकर कूड़ेदान में डाल देती।\nगाँव और ज़्यादा साफ़ रहने लगा। और चीकू का बादल और छोटा होने लगा।\nफिर एक दिन वो गायब हो गया।\nएकदम चला गया।\nऔर चीकू शायद दुनिया की सबसे ख़ुश लड़की हो गई।\nउसके बाद चीकू ने कूड़ा नहीं फैलाया।\nसच तो यह है कि उसे भी साफ़ गाँव में रहना अच्छा लगता था।\nलेकिन वह डरती कि कहीं कचरे का बादल फिर न आ जाए।\nचलो अब हम कचरे की बात करें!\nकभी सोचा है कि जो कचरा हम कूड़ेदान में फेंक देते है उसका क्या होता होगा? नहीं, वह हमारे सिर पर बादल बन कर नहीं मँडराता लेकिन जो भी कचरा हम फेंकते है वो हमारे घर के पास बने बड़े से कचराघर में जमा हो जाता है। सब कुछ एक साथ, सड़ती सब्जियाँ, टॉफ़ी के रैपर, किताबों-कापियों के फटे पन्ने।\nजब भी हम केले के छिलके या पेंसिल की छीलन सड़क पर फेंकते है, तो यह कचरा सड़क के किनारे इकठ्ठा हो जाता है। कुछ उन नालियों के अंदर चला जाता है और उन में जमा हो जाता है। रूकी हुई नालियों में मक्खी-मच्छर पैदा होते हैं जो बीमारियाँ फैलाते हैं! इससे हमारा पर्यावरण गन्दा होता है और अपने आसपास कूड़ा- कचरा तो किसी को भी अच्छा नहीं लगता। चीकू के दिल से पूछिये।\nकचरा फैलने से कैसे रोकें\n-  कूड़ा-कचरा बिल्कुल न बिखेरें। हमेशा, कूड़ेदान में ही डालें।\n-  सुबह स्कूल जाते समय अगर रास्ते में केला खाते हैं\nतो उसका छिलका सड़क पर न फेंके ।\n- छिलका रखने के लिए माँ या पापा से एक छोटा लिफ़ाफ़ा ले जाईये, स्कूल पहुँचने के बाद याद से छिलके को कूड़ेदान में डाल दीजिये।\n- केले वाले लिफ़ाफ़े की तरह कई चीज़ें आपको बेकार लगती होंगी, लेकिन सब चीज़ें बेकार नहीं होतीं। छिलके के साथ लिफ़ाफ़े को बिल्कुल नहीं फेंकना, उसे वापस घर ले जाकर दोबारा इस्तेमाल कीजिये।\n- कूड़ेदान को ढक दीजिये जिससे उस में मक्खियाँ बिलकुल न पहुँच पाएँ।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":23,"title":"कचरे का बादल"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-25-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कचरे का बादल","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:25","title":"कचरे का बादल","author":"Karanjeet Kaur","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Karanjeet Kaur\nIllustrator: Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi\nTranslator: Poonam S. Kudesia\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: कचरे का बादल is translated by Poonam S. Kudesia . The © for this translation lies with Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' A Cloud of Trash ' , by Karanjeet Kaur . © Pratham Books , 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nOther Credits:\nThis book was first published on StoryWeaver by Pratham Books. The development of this book has been supported by Oracle. Art Director: Vinayak Varma\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: A girl running away from a cloud of waste , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: A sad girl , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: A girl being teased in school , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: A girl looking at a cloud of trash , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: A girl hiding behind a bench , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: A sad, lonely girl , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: A girl littering , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: An unhappy girl , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: A girl looking scared from under a blanket , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: A girl trying to get rid of trash , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThe development of this book has been supported by Oracle.\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: A girl crushing a plastic bottle , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: A girl scolding a boy for littering , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: A girl eating at the table, a woman throwing away plastic bags , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 14: A girl picking up trash from the street , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 15: A cheerful girl playing , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 16: Children playing with balloons and a kite , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 17: A girl crying , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 18: A girl standing behind a trash bin , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 19: Mixed trash , by Bhavana Vyas Vipparthi © Pratham Books, 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThe development of this book has been supported by Oracle.\nकचरे का बादल (Hindi)\nचीकू के सिर पर कचरे का बादल मँडरा रहा है जिसकी वजह से वह दुनिया की सबसे दुखी लड़की हो गई। यह शानदार कहानी पढ़िए और जानिए कि चीकू ने कचरे के डरावने बादल से छुटकारा कैसे पाया।\nयह पठन स्तर २ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो सरल शब्द पढ़ लेते हैं और थोड़ी मदद से नए शब्द भी पढ़ सकते हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%9a%e0%a4%b0%e0%a5%87-%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%be-%e0%a4%ac%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a6%e0%a4%b2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"063f0d3c37bd1021"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"कचरे का बादल\nअपनी सारी दोस्तों के बीच चीकू बहुत दुखी थी।\nवो अपनी क्लास की सबसे दुखी लड़की थी।\nशायद वो दुनिया की सबसे दुखी लड़की थी।\nदोस्त? चीकू का अब कोई दोस्त नहीं था।\nचीकू के साथ कोई खेलना नहीं चाहता था।\nक्योंकि उसके सिर पर हमेशा एक बादल मँडराता।\nकचरे का एक बादल ।\nसंतरे के छिलके और बिस्कुट के खाली लिफ़ाफ़े,\nटूटे खिलौने, और पेंसिल की छीलन,\nप्लास्टिक की टेढ़ी-मेढ़ी बोतलें,\nऔर रंग-बिरँगी थैलियाँ,\nऔर इन सब पर भिनभिनाते मक्खियों के झुंड।\nकोई भी बच्चा ऐसी लड़की के साथ नहीं खेलना चाहता था जिसके सिर पर हमेशा कचरे का बादल मँडराता हो।\nकहीं कोई केले का छिल्का उसके सर पर गिर पड़े तो? छी!\nचीकू तो छुपम-छुपाई तक भी नहीं खेल सकती थी।\nक्योंकि बादल उसका पता बता देता था।\nएक दिन वो सोना से बोली, \"हम साथ-साथ स्कूल चलते हैं।\" सोना तो फ़ौरन दूर भाग गई।\n\"क्या मैं तुम्हारा पेंसिल शार्पनर इस्तेमाल कर लूँ?\" उसने स्वीटी से पूछा।\nस्वीटी मुँह चिढ़ाते हुए अपनी जगह बदल कर आशा के पास बैठ गई।\nचीकू को खाना भी अकेले खाना पड़ा।\nचीकू जानती थी कि उसे अम्मा का कहना मानना  चाहिए था।\nअम्मा हमेशा उसे कूड़ा फैलाने से मना करती थी।\n\"सड़क पर केले का  छिलका मत फेंको।\"\n\"बिस्कुट के खाली लिफ़ाफ़े कूड़ेदान में डालो।\"\nलेकिन चीकू ने उनकी बात नहीं मानी। वह हँसती रही और कूड़ा फैलाती रही।\nफिर एक दिन अम्मा को बहुत गुस्सा आ गया, उसने कहा, \"देखना अब यह कूड़ा हमेशा तुम्हारे साथ ही रहेगा!\" चीकू हँसती रही।\nअगले दिन जब चीकू सो कर उठी तो चारों तरफ मक्खियाँ भिनभिना रही थी, हर तरफ बदबू ही बदबू थी।\nसाथ ही सिर पर कचरे का बादल मँडरा रहा था।\nअम्मा की बात सच साबित हुई और उसके बाद चीकू हँसना बस भूल ही गई!\nचीकू ने भागना चाहा ।\nलेकिन कचरे का वो बादल हर जगह उसका पीछा करता रहा ।\nचीकू ने एक झाड़ू लेकर बादल को हटाने की कोशिश की,\nलेकिन वह उसे हटा नहीं सकी ।\nचीकू ने भरपूर कोशिश की!\nउसने चीख-चीख कर बादल से हटने को कहा।\nउसने तो बादल को कूड़ेदान में फेंकने की भी\nकोशिश की।\nलेकिन कचरे का बादल हटा ही नहीं।\nतब चीकू हो गयी बहुत दुखी।\nइसके बाद चीकू ने बाला को देखा सड़क पर केले का छिलका फेंकते हुए।\nचीकू को गुस्सा आ गया। क्या बाला को मेरे सिर पर कचरे का बादल नहीं दिख रहा?\nवो चिल्लाई, \"अरे बुदधू, छिलके को सड़क पर मत फेंको, कोई फिसल जाएगा!\"\nकचरे के बादल से डर कर, बाला ने, छिलके को कूड़ेदान में फेंक दिया।\nअगले दिन, कचरे का वह बादल थोड़ा सा छोटा हो गया!\nचीकू ने सोचा, \"अरे ऐसा कैसे हुआ?\"\nफिर चीकू ने देखा, कि रमा आंटी, प्लास्टिक की थैलियों को फेंक रहीं थीं।\nचीकू ने कहा, \"आंटी, थैलियों को उठाकर दोबारा इस्तेमाल कीजिए।\"\nरीमा आंटी थैलियाँ उठाकर वहाँ से चली गई! अगले दिन जब चीकू सो कर उठी, तो बादल और भी छोटा हो गया था।चीकू मुस्कराई, वह समझ गई थी कि उसे क्या करना है।\nफिर जब भी कोई बिस्कुट का पैकेट/लिफ़ाफ़ा या पेंसिल की छीलन फेंकता चीकू उसे रोक देती।\nप्लास्टिक की हर बेकार बोतल उठाकर कूड़ेदान में डाल देती।\nगाँव और ज़्यादा साफ़ रहने लगा। और चीकू का बादल और छोटा होने लगा।\nफिर एक दिन वो गायब हो गया।\nएकदम चला गया।\nऔर चीकू शायद दुनिया की सबसे ख़ुश लड़की हो गई।\nउसके बाद चीकू ने कूड़ा नहीं फैलाया।\nसच तो यह है कि उसे भी साफ़ गाँव में रहना अच्छा लगता था।\nलेकिन वह डरती कि कहीं कचरे का बादल फिर न आ जाए।\nचलो अब हम कचरे की बात करें!\nकभी सोचा है कि जो कचरा हम कूड़ेदान में फेंक देते है उसका क्या होता होगा? नहीं, वह हमारे सिर पर बादल बन कर नहीं मँडराता लेकिन जो भी कचरा हम फेंकते है वो हमारे घर के पास बने बड़े से कचराघर में जमा हो जाता है। सब कुछ एक साथ, सड़ती सब्जियाँ, टॉफ़ी के रैपर, किताबों-कापियों के फटे पन्ने।\nजब भी हम केले के छिलके या पेंसिल की छीलन सड़क पर फेंकते है, तो यह कचरा सड़क के किनारे इकठ्ठा हो जाता है। कुछ उन नालियों के अंदर चला जाता है और उन में जमा हो जाता है। रूकी हुई नालियों में मक्खी-मच्छर पैदा होते हैं जो बीमारियाँ फैलाते हैं! इससे हमारा पर्यावरण गन्दा होता है और अपने आसपास कूड़ा- कचरा तो किसी को भी अच्छा नहीं लगता। चीकू के दिल से पूछिये।\nकचरा फैलने से कैसे रोकें\n-  कूड़ा-कचरा बिल्कुल न बिखेरें। हमेशा, कूड़ेदान में ही डालें।\n-  सुबह स्कूल जाते समय अगर रास्ते में केला खाते हैं\nतो उसका छिलका सड़क पर न फेंके ।\n- छिलका रखने के लिए माँ या पापा से एक छोटा लिफ़ाफ़ा ले जाईये, स्कूल पहुँचने के बाद याद से छिलके को कूड़ेदान में डाल दीजिये।\n- केले वाले लिफ़ाफ़े की तरह कई चीज़ें आपको बेकार लगती होंगी, लेकिन सब चीज़ें बेकार नहीं होतीं। छिलके के साथ लिफ़ाफ़े को बिल्कुल नहीं फेंकना, उसे वापस घर ले जाकर दोबारा इस्तेमाल कीजिये।\n- कूड़ेदान को ढक दीजिये जिससे उस में मक्खियाँ बिलकुल न पहुँच पाएँ।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":24,"title":"कचरे का बादल"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-26-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कछुआ और खरगोश","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:26","title":"कछुआ और खरगोश","author":"Venkatramana Gowda","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Venkatramana Gowda\nIllustrator: Padmanabh\nTranslator: K. Vijaya\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: कछुआ और खरगोश is translated by K. Vijaya . The © for this translation lies with Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' ಮೊಲ ಮತ್ತು ಆಮೆ ' , by Venkatramana Gowda . © Pratham Books , 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nOther Credits:\nThis book has been published on StoryWeaver by Pratham Books.'The Hare and The Tortoise (Again!)' has been published by Pratham Books in partnership with the Rajiv Gandhi Foundation. Pratham Books is a not-for-profit organization that publishes books in multiple Indian languages to promote reading among children. www.prathambooks.org\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: Tortoise with a scroll on the back of the hare , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: Animal Kingdom , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: Trees and Rolling Plains , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Tortoise looking at Rabbit eating Carrots , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: Lion thinking of the Hare and the Tortoise , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: Hare and the Tortoise , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: Lion making a gesture , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: Hare and Tortoise thinking of river and rocks , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Hare and Tortoise thinking of each other on each other's backs , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Tortoise with a scroll on the back of a rabbit , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: Tortoise swimming across the river with rabbit on the back holding a scroll , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: Tortoise and Hare speaking to a Lion , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: Tortoise and Hare running and singing , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 14: Tortoise on Hare's back and Hare on Tortoise's back , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 15: Tortoise looking at Rabbit eating Carrots - for coloring , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 16: Animal Kingdom - for coloring , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nकछुआ और खरगोश (Hindi)\nबहुत दिनों पहले कछुए ने अपनी लगन के बल पर घमण्डी खरगोश को दौड़ में हराया था। अब दोनों फिर साथ आये हैं और उन्हें मिल कर राजा का ज़रूरी काम करना है। सहयोग के बिना यह असम्भव है पर क्या दोनों विरोधी मिल कर काम कर पायेंगे?\nयह पठन स्तर ३ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो खुद पढ़ने को तैयार हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%9b%e0%a5%81%e0%a4%86-%e0%a4%94%e0%a4%b0-%e0%a4%96%e0%a4%b0%e0%a4%97%e0%a5%8b%e0%a4%b6-2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"dc4ee4afb72521e2"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"कछुआ और खरगोश\nकछुए और खरगोश की दौड़ तो याद है न? उस दौड़ के बाद जानवरों के पूरे राज्य में सभी कछुए और खरगोश के बारे में चर्चा करने लगे। जहाँ देखो, उन्हीं की बात होती थी।\nदौड़ में कुछ आलस के कारण खरगोश हार गया। अपनी मंज़िल की ओर लगातार चलकर कछुआ विजयी हुआ, लेकिन जंगल की प्रजा में दोनों के लिए कोई भेदभाव नहीं था। दोनों की ही बहुत इज्ज़त होती।\nअपनी जीत पर कछुआ इतराया नहीं। अपनी हार पर खरगोश ने अपमानित महसूस नहीं किया, न ही कछुए के प्रति जलन महसूस की।\nकुछ दिनों बाद उस जंगल के राजा को पड़ोसी जंगल के राजा के साथ ज़रूरी काम पड़ा। उनकी बातचीत तुरंत होनी ज़रूरी थी। लेकिन राजा को फुर्सत नहीं मिल रही थी। और कामों में उलझे होने के कारण उसके लिये पड़ोसी राज्य जाना संभव नहीं था।\nअतः राजा ने खरगोश और कछुए को अपना प्रतिनिधि बनाकर वहाँ भेजने की सोची।\n\"तुम दोनों में से किसी एक को पड़ोसी राज्य जाना पड़ेगा। मेरा संदेश उन्हें देकर उनका जवाब लेकर एक दिन के अन्दर वापस आना होगा।\"\nपड़ोसी राज्य पहुँचने का रास्ता बहुत कठिन था। काँटों और पत्थरों से भरा था। बीच में दो नदियाँ भी पड़ती थीं। चाहे कछुआ हो या खरगोश रास्ता आसानी से तय होने वाला नहीं था। और एक ही दिन में तो वह रास्ता तय करना असंभव ही था।\nतब खरगोश और कछुए ने एक साथ बैठकर बहुत सोचा। हम दोनों में से किसी एक से यह काम न होगा इसीलिए दोनों साथ मिलकर चलेंगे। जंगल के रास्ते पर खरगोश अपनी पीठ पर कछुए को बिठाकर दौड़ लगाएगा। नदी पार करते समय खरगोश कछुए की पीठ पर चढ़ जायेगा। यह तय करके दोनों को तसल्ली हुई।\nअगले दिन तड़के दोनों तैयार हो गये। राजा का संदेश लेकर दोनों निकल पड़े। खरगोश अपनी पीठ पर कछुए को बिठाकर तेज़ी से दौड़ा।\nरास्ते में नदी आई। तब कछुए ने खरगोश को अपनी पीठ पर बिठाकर नदी पार कराई। फिर से खरगोश ने कछुए को पीठ पर बिठाकर दौड़ लगाई। दूसरी नदी आते ही कछुए ने अपना काम किया।\nइस तरह दोनों साथ मिलकर बहुत जल्दी अपनी मंज़िल तक पहुँच गये। उस राजा से बातचीत करके वापस लौटे।\nजितना समय उनके राजा ने दिया था उससे पहले ही दोनों ने अपना काम कर दिखाया।\nइस चित्र में रंग भरो।\nइस चित्र में रंग भरो।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":25,"title":"कछुआ और खरगोश"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-27-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कछुआ और खरगोश","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:27","title":"कछुआ और खरगोश","author":"Venkatramana Gowda","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Venkatramana Gowda\nIllustrator: Padmanabh\nTranslator: K. Vijaya\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: कछुआ और खरगोश is translated by K. Vijaya . The © for this translation lies with Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' ಮೊಲ ಮತ್ತು ಆಮೆ ' , by Venkatramana Gowda . © Pratham Books , 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nOther Credits:\nThis book has been published on StoryWeaver by Pratham Books.'The Hare and The Tortoise (Again!)' has been published by Pratham Books in partnership with the Rajiv Gandhi Foundation. Pratham Books is a not-for-profit organization that publishes books in multiple Indian languages to promote reading among children. www.prathambooks.org\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: Tortoise with a scroll on the back of the hare , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: Animal Kingdom , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: Trees and Rolling Plains , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Tortoise looking at Rabbit eating Carrots , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: Lion thinking of the Hare and the Tortoise , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: Hare and the Tortoise , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: Lion making a gesture , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: Hare and Tortoise thinking of river and rocks , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Hare and Tortoise thinking of each other on each other's backs , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Tortoise with a scroll on the back of a rabbit , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: Tortoise swimming across the river with rabbit on the back holding a scroll , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: Tortoise and Hare speaking to a Lion , by Padmanabh © Pratham Books, 2004. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: Tortoise and Hare running a