: People talking to man carrying bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: Sad man with bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: Man going to town , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: Man travelling with bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Man taking bananas from tree , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: People looking at man with bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: People looking at man , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: Cows looking at man with bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: People staring at man with bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 14: People at religious ceremony , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 15: Priest talking to confused man , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 16: Men talking , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 17: Two men talking , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 18: Religious ritual with priest and people , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 19: Scared man during religious ritual , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 20: People staring at man with bag , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 21: Priest looking at man with bag , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 22: Man offering priest a sweet , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 23: Man thinking of bananas and packets , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 24: Surprised priest and laughing child , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 25: Priest and people laughing , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 26: Children looking at man with bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 27: Man wheeling a pile of bananas , by Angie & Upesh © Pratham Books, 2010. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nकहानी केलों की! (Hindi)\nश्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास के खेतों में बढ़िया मीठे केले उगते थे। पर कोई भी उन्हें खाना नहीं चाहता था। इस मीठी कहानी को पढ़ कर पता लगाइये कि श्रिंगेरी ने केलों का क्या किया।\nयह पठन स्तर २ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो सरल शब्द पढ़ लेते हैं और थोड़ी मदद से नए शब्द भी पढ़ सकते हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%b9%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a8%e0%a5%80-%e0%a4%95%e0%a5%87%e0%a4%b2%e0%a5%8b%e0%a4%82-%e0%a4%95%e0%a5%80/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"d5d348b99edd6ba9"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"कहानी केलों की!\nश्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास आज परेशान था।\nकिसी को भी उसके खेत के मीठे केले नहीं चाहिये थे।\nउसके घरवालों को नहीं।\nउसके पड़ोसी को नहीं।\nउसके दोस्तों को नहीं।\nउन व्यापारियों को नहीं जो दूर बाज़ार में उन्हें बेच सकते थे।\nऔर तो और, उसकी गायों को भी नहीं।\nवे सभी बोले, “धन्यवाद, अब और नहीं। केले बड़े मीठे हैं पर हम बहुत खा चुके। अब और नहीं खा सकते!” बेचारा श्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास!\nअब इस बढ़िया केले की फ़सल का वह क्या करे?\nउसने सोचा गाँव के पास जो बड़ा शहर डोड्डुरू है वहाँ किसान केन्द्र से मदद माँगी जाये।\nसबसे बढ़िया केले गाड़ी पर लाद कर वह चल पड़ा।\nज़रूर कोई न कोई उसे एक अच्छा सुझाव देगा।\nकुछ दिनों बाद श्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास खुशी-खुशी घर लौटा।\nउसने खेतों में फिर से केले उगाये।\nपर इस बार उसने किसी को भी केले नहीं दिये।\nअपने घरवालों को नहीं।\nअपने पड़ोसी को नहीं।\nअपने दोस्तों को नहीं।\nउन व्यापारियों को नहीं जो दूर बाज़ार में उन केलों को बेच सकते थे।\nऔर हाँ, अपनी गायों को भी नहीं!\nसबका माथा ठनका।\nकेले आखिर कहाँ जा रहे थे?\nएक दिन उसके पड़ोसी शिवन्ना ने बड़ी सी पूजा का आयोजन किया।\nपंडित जी ने कहा कि भगवान को चढ़ाने के लिये 108 पके केले ले के आओ।\nशिवन्ना दौड़ा-दौड़ा श्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास के पास पहुँचा। “पहले मना करने के लिये माफ़ी चाहता हूँ पर अब मुझे 108 पके केले चाहियें। मेरी मदद करोगे?”\nश्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास ने ज़रा सोचा।\n“वैसे तो मेरी फ़सल अब कट चुकी है पर देखता हूँ शायद कुछ हो सके। तुम अपनी पूजा शुरू करो। मैं ज़रूर पहुँच जाऊँगा।”\nपूजा शुरू हो गई।\nसभी गाँववाले देखने आये।\nपंडित जी ने मंत्र पढ़े।\nजल्द ही वह समय आ गया जब भगवान को केले चढ़ाने थे।\nतभी श्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास एक बड़ा सा थैला ले के वहाँ पहुँचा।\nथैले में से उसने 27 पैकेट निकाल कर पवित्र अग्नि के आस-पास रख दिये। हर पैकेट अच्छे से केले के पत्ते में लिपटा हुआ था।\nहर पैकेट पे लिखा थाः “उच्च कोटि केले का हलवा-एस एस फ़ार्म्स”\nश्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास ने एक पैकेट पंडित जी को दिया।\n“हरेक पैकेट में 4 केलों का गूदा है। तो ये रहे आपके 108 पके केले!”\nकुल 27 पैकेट हैं।\nपंडित जी का मुँह खुला का खुला रह गया। बेचारे मंत्र बोलना भी भूल गये!\nसन्नाटे में एक बच्चे ने किलकारी मारी!\nकुछ ही देर में सभी गाँव वाले भी हँसते-हँसते ताली बजा रहे थे।\nअब सभी को पता है कि श्रिंगेरी श्रीनिवास अपने केले की फसल का क्या करता है।\nक्या आप जानते हैं?\nबनाना यानि अंग्रेज़ी में केले का नाम अरबी भाषा में “अंगुली” के नाम से आता है।\nविश्‍व भर में भारत केलों का सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है। यहाँ खाने योग्य 120 किस्म के केले उगते है।\nट्रिची में नैशनल रिसर्च सेन्टर ऑन बनानाज़ में 1120 केले की किस्में हैं।\nकेलों में खनिज हैं जो दिमाग की शक्ति बढ़ाते हैं। केले से विद्यार्थियों को स्फूर्ति मिलती है।\nकई भारतीय मिठाइयाँ केलों से बनती हैं- केरल में केला पायसम, कर्नाटक में केला रसायना, केले का हलवा, रवा केला- गुड़ की मिठाई। क्या आप और मिठाइयों के नाम जानते हैं?"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":38,"title":"कहानी केलों की!"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-40-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:40","title":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे","author":"Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"\nIllustrator: Debasmita Dasgupta\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: कहानी- गजानन गंजे is written by Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\" . © Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\" , 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: A monk sleeping on the floor , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: A monk sleeping on the floor , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Two monks standing together in a garden and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: Two monks standing together and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: Two monks standing together in a garden and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Two monks standing together in a garden and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nकहानी- गजानन गंजे (Hindi)\nगजानन बीमार हुए और बाल उड़ गए. तब उन्हों ने क्या उपाय किया ?\nयह पठन स्तर १ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो पढ़ना शुरू कर रहे हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%b9%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a8%e0%a5%80-%e0%a4%97%e0%a4%9c%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a8%e0%a4%a8-%e0%a4%97%e0%a4%82%e0%a4%9c%e0%a5%87-2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"01d9fc9ea86609a2"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे\nगंजा गजानन\nओमप्रकाश क्षत्रिय \"प्रकाश\"\nगजानन को एक बीमारी लगी .\nवह गंजा हो गया.\nवह गुरूजी के पास गया. गुरूजी हिरण को घुमा रहे थे.\nगजानन ने कहा, \" गुरूजी ! मेरे बाल उड़ गए हैं. उन्हें उगाने का उपाए बताइए.\"\nगुरूजी बोले, \" गजानन ! तुम गंजे ही अच्छे लग रहे हो.\"\n\" नहीं गुरूजी ! मुझे उपाय बताइए .\"\nगजानन ने जिद कीं .\n\" गुरूजी ! उपाय बता दीजिए ,\" तोता बोला.\n\"तो सुनिए,\" गुरूजी ने कहा.\n\"मेरी तरह बालों वाली टोपी ( विग ) लगा लीजिए,\" कहते हुए गुरूजी ने अपने माथे का विग हटा दिया."}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":39,"title":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-41-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:41","title":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे","author":"Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"\nIllustrator: Debasmita Dasgupta\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: कहानी- गजानन गंजे is written by Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\" . © Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\" , 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: A monk sleeping on the floor , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: A monk sleeping on the floor , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Two monks standing together in a garden and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: Two monks standing together and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: Two monks standing together in a garden and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Buddha in confusion and thinking on some questions , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Two monks standing together in a garden and smiling , by Debasmita Dasgupta © Pratham Books, 2016. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nकहानी- गजानन गंजे (Hindi)\nगजानन बीमार हुए और बाल उड़ गए. तब उन्हों ने क्या उपाय किया ?\nयह पठन स्तर १ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो पढ़ना शुरू कर रहे हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%b9%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a8%e0%a5%80-%e0%a4%97%e0%a4%9c%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a8%e0%a4%a8-%e0%a4%97%e0%a4%82%e0%a4%9c%e0%a5%87/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"01d9fc9ea86609a2"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे\nगंजा गजानन\nओमप्रकाश क्षत्रिय \"प्रकाश\"\nगजानन को एक बीमारी लगी .\nवह गंजा हो गया.\nवह गुरूजी के पास गया. गुरूजी हिरण को घुमा रहे थे.\nगजानन ने कहा, \" गुरूजी ! मेरे बाल उड़ गए हैं. उन्हें उगाने का उपाए बताइए.\"\nगुरूजी बोले, \" गजानन ! तुम गंजे ही अच्छे लग रहे हो.\"\n\" नहीं गुरूजी ! मुझे उपाय बताइए .\"\nगजानन ने जिद कीं .\n\" गुरूजी ! उपाय बता दीजिए ,\" तोता बोला.\n\"तो सुनिए,\" गुरूजी ने कहा.\n\"मेरी तरह बालों वाली टोपी ( विग ) लगा लीजिए,\" कहते हुए गुरूजी ने अपने माथे का विग हटा दिया."}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":40,"title":"कहानी- गजानन गंजे"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-42-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कहानी- बादल की सैर","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:42","title":"कहानी- बादल की सैर","author":"Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"\nIllustrator: Ajit Narayan\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: कहानी- बादल की सैर is written by Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\" . © Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\" , 2017. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nIllustration Attributions:\nCover page: Fish looking up at the cloud in the sky , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 2: Blue cloud over a hill , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: Blue cloud over a hill , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: Blue cloud over a hill , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: Blue cloud over a hill , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: Blue cloud over a hill , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: Blue cloud in the sky , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: Fish looking up at the cloud in the sky , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: Fish looking up at the cloud in the sky , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Fish looking up at the cloud in the sky , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 11: Fish leaping out of a pond as it rains , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 12: Fish leaping out of a pond as it rains , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 13: Falling rain , by Ajit Narayan © Pratham Books, 2007. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nकहानी- बादल की सैर (Hindi)\nबादल घुमने चला. उसे कौन-कौन मिला ? फिर वह क्या करने लगा ?\nयह पठन स्तर १ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो पढ़ना शुरू कर रहे हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a4%b9%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a8%e0%a5%80-%e0%a4%ac%e0%a4%be%e0%a4%a6%e0%a4%b2-%e0%a4%95%e0%a5%80-%e0%a4%b8%e0%a5%88%e0%a4%b0-2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"ebe76e93e50e56b4"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"कहानी- बादल की सैर\nएक बादल घुमने चला.\nसाथ में चिड़िया भी उड़ती\nहुई चली.\n\" चलो ! तेज़ी से उडो.\"\nबादल ने चिड़िया से कहा .\nचिड़िया थक कर पहाड़ पर बैठ गई.\n\" तुम जाओ ! मैं तुम्हारे साथ नहीं उड़ सकती.\"\n\" ठीक है  ,\" कहते हुए\nबादल तेज़ी से आगे बढ़ गया.\nवह जंगल के ऊपर से जा रहा था .\nउसे देख कर फल, फूल,\nपौधे, पेड़ और भंवरे नाचने लगे.\nवह नदी के ऊपर से गुजरा.\nनदी में मीनू मछली रहती थी.\nवह बोली, \" आओ\nना  बादल भाई !\n\" मैं तो घुमने जा रहा हूँ. यहाँ\nरुक कर क्या करूंगा ?\"\nबादल ने मीनू से पूछा .\n\" हम-तुम मिल कर खेलेंगे.\" मीनू  ने\nकहा.\nबादल को मीनू\nकी बात अच्छी लगी.\nवह बरस कर\nखेलने लगा ."}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":41,"title":"कहानी- बादल की सैर"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-43-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"कहानी- बादल की सैर","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:43","title":"कहानी- बादल की सैर","author":"Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Omprakash Kshatriya \"Prakash\"\nIllust