portion of a child's face , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 3: A young boy's wide-eyed face , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 4: A child with closed eyes , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 5: A child with puffed up cheeks , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 6: A pair of eyes partially hidden by a pink object , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 7: A girl and her dog watching something fly away , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 8: A girl looking surprised , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 9: A boy and dog watching a balloon fly by , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 10: Puzzled girl , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nIllustration Attributions:\nPage 11: A boy holding a piece of string , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Page 12: A girl, a boy and a dog looking at a deflated balloon , by Shailja Jain Chougule © Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Disclaimer: https://www.storyweaver.org.in/terms_and_conditions\nSome rights reserved. This book is CC­-BY­-4.0 licensed. You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission. For full terms of use and attribution, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nक्यों भई क्यों? (Hindi)\nएक छोटी सी बच्ची की आँखें लाल क्यों हैं? यह कहानी पढ़ने के बाद नन्हे-मुन्ने पाठक भी गोल-गोल मुँह बनाना चाहेंगे।\nयह पठन स्तर १ की किताब है, उन बच्चों के लिए जो पढ़ना शुरू कर रहे हैं।\nPratham Books goes digital to weave a whole new chapter in the realm of multilingual children's stories. Knitting together children, authors, illustrators and publishers. Folding in teachers, and translators. To create a rich fabric of openly licensed multilingual stories for the children of India ­­ and the world. Our unique online platform, StoryWeaver, is a playground where children, parents, teachers and librarians can get creative. Come, start weaving today, and help us get a book in every child's hand!","provenance":"Exact Hindi text reconstructed from cached official GDL EPUB extract; source fidelity only, with no native-speaker quality claim.","rights":"licensed","licenseNote":"CC BY 4.0; attribution retained in this source record.","authorship":"licensed","url":"https://content.digitallibrary.io/hi/book/%e0%a4%95%e0%a5%8d%e0%a4%af%e0%a5%8b%e0%a4%82-%e0%a4%ad%e0%a4%88-%e0%a4%95%e0%a5%8d%e0%a4%af%e0%a5%8b%e0%a4%82-2/","edition":"GDL Hindi CC BY 4.0"},"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewedBy":"prepare-hi-gdl-collection source-fidelity check","reviewedAt":"2026-10-01","notes":"Source fidelity review only; no native-speaker quality claim.","contentSignature":"ee277e541f5f0662"},"topics":[],"editorialTags":[],"prepTargets":[],"generated":false,"quality":{"checkedWith":"quality@1","flags":[],"verdict":"clean"},"sections":[{"paragraphs":[{"text":"क्यों भई क्यों?\nआँखें लाल हैं।\nक्यों भई क्यों?\nनाक बह रही है।\nपोंछो, इसे साफ़ करो।\nगाल गर्म हो गए हैं।\nइन्हें मत छुओ!\nगला पक सा गया है।\nपास में पानी भी नहीं है!\nमुँह गोल हो रहा है।\nक्यों भई क्यों?\nसारी हवा निकल गई।\nक्यों भई क्यों?\nअब, हम क्या करें?\nधागा लाओ\nगुब्बारा बाँधो।\nतुम गुब्बारा फुलाओ।\nअब तुम्हारी बारी।"}]}],"work":{"slug":"gdl-hindi-ccby","courseId":"india-hi","chapter":{"index":51,"title":"क्यों भई क्यों?"}},"streams":["children"]},{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"gdl-53-ch01","lang":"hi","title":"क्यों भई क्यों?","contentType":"story","corpus":{"id":"gdl-hindi-ccby","kind":"comprehensible-input","title":"Global Digital Library Hindi CC BY collection"},"source":{"id":"src:hi:gdl:53","title":"क्यों भई क्यों?","author":"Richa Bhaskar","publisher":"StoryWeaver","attribution":"Author: Richa Bhaskar\nIllustrator: Shailja Jain Chougule\nTranslator: Arti Smit\nThis book was made possible by Pratham Books' StoryWeaver platform. Content under Creative Commons licenses can be downloaded, translated and can even be used to create new stories ­ provided you give appropriate credit, and indicate if changes were made. To know more about this, and the full terms of use and attribution, please visit the following link .\nStory Attribution:\nThis story: क्यों भई क्यों? is translated by Arti Smit . The © for this translation lies with Pratham Books, 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license. Based on Original story: ' Why, Oh Why! ' , by Richa Bhaskar . © Pratham Books , 2015. Some rights reserved. Released under CC BY 4.0 license.\nOther Credits:\nThis book has been published on StoryWeaver by Pratham Books. It was developed in a workshop of authors and illustrators organized by Pratham Books. The development of the print 